# The inventory snapshot is 74.7 MB of real filesystem paths -- every project
# name, document title and profile directory on the machine that produced it.
# It is a test fixture, not source, and it must never be committed.
tests/gold/inventory-*.tsv
tests/gold/candidates*.tsv

# The four answer keys written against the real corpus. Each names actual
# files -- artwork titles, document authors, wiki page names -- and each is
# needed ONLY by HOMEGRAPH_REAL_CORPUS=1. The default synthetic corpus carries
# its own keys, declared in tests/fixtures/synthetic.py, which is source.
tests/gold/gold-set.tsv
tests/gold/cp2-links.tsv
tests/gold/cp3-documents.tsv
tests/gold/cp4-filenames.tsv

# The rest of the real-corpus apparatus, held out for the same reason and not
# a smaller one. `real_corpus.py` holds each checkpoint's thresholds and the
# paths they are measured at; the samplers name the project directories they
# drew from. All four are needed only by HOMEGRAPH_REAL_CORPUS=1, every
# checkpoint refuses with a clear message when they are absent, and nothing in
# the default synthetic path touches them.
tests/gold/real_corpus.py
tests/gold/sample_gold.py
tests/gold/sample_gold_round2.py
tests/gold/sample_gold_round3.py

# Generated stores, scratch space and rendered graphs
.homegraph/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
graph.html

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
